+# Time Tracker Library - Contract
+
+## Behaviors & Verification
+
+### C1: Starting a named timer
+- **Behavior:** Starting a timer with a valid name creates a new entry with that name, records the start time, and stores it.
+- **Verify:** Start timer named "work", then get entries — should have 1 entry with name "work", start is a number (Date.now()), no stop property.
+
+### C2: Starting a timer auto-stops previous
+- **Behavior:** Starting a new timer while one is running stops the previous one (sets its stop time) before starting the new one.
+- **Verify:** Start "work", start "break" — the "work" entry should have a stop time, and "break" entry should not.
+
+### C3: Stopping a running timer
+- **Behavior:** Stopping sets the stop time on the currently running entry.
+- **Verify:** Start "work", stop — the "work" entry should have a stop time. Timer count should still be 1.
+
+### C4: Stopping when nothing is running throws
+- **Behavior:** Calling stop when no timer is running throws an error.
+- **Verify:** Call stop() on a fresh tracker — should throw Error.
+
+### C5: Starting with empty name throws
+- **Behavior:** Starting a timer with an empty string (or whitespace-only) throws an error.
+- **Verify:** start("") throws, start("   ") throws.
+
+### C6: Persistence — entries survive tracker recreation
+- **Behavior:** When a tracker is created with a file path, entries written to it are reloaded when a new tracker instance reads the same file.
+- **Verify:** Create tracker1, start "work", stop. Create tracker2 with same path, get entries — should have the "work" entry.
+
+### C7: Persistence — file and parent dirs created automatically
+- **Behavior:** If the file path includes directories that don't exist, they are created automatically.
+- **Verify:** Use path like "/tmp/deep/nested/dir/times.json" — the file should be created without error.
+
+### C8: Query all entries
+- **Behavior:** `getEntries()` returns all stored entries in order.
+- **Verify:** Start "a", stop, start "b", stop — getEntries returns 2 entries.
+
+### C9: Filter entries by date range
+- **Behavior:** `getEntries({ start: Date, end: Date })` returns only entries whose start time falls within that range.
+- **Verify:** Create entries at known times, filter with a range — only matching entries returned.
+
+### C10: Summary of time per task
+- **Behavior:** `getSummary()` returns a record mapping task names to total milliseconds. Running tasks use current time for duration.
+- **Verify:** Start "work", wait 10ms, start "break", wait 5ms, stop. Summary has work > 0, break > 0. Multiple entries with same name are summed.
+
+### C11: Unicode support
+- **Behavior:** Task names with emoji and unicode characters work correctly as task names.
+- **Verify:** Start and stop timers with names like "🚀 launch", "日本語" — entries store and retrieve them correctly.
+
+### C12: Configurable file path
+- **Behavior:** The file path for persistence is configurable via constructor/options.
+- **Verify:** Two trackers with different paths don't interfere.
